WEBVTT

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:13.559
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> ‘I’ve found where she lives,’

00:00:14.015 --> 00:00:16.027
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> said the detective quietly.

00:00:16.812 --> 00:00:18.051
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> ‘Here is the address.’

00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:21.005
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> Hartley took the piece of paper.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.020
On it were the words,

00:00:23.143 --> 00:00:28.253
‘Vivienne Arlington, number 341 East 49th Street.’

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:30.924
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> ‘She moved there a week ago,’

00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:32.637
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> said the detective.

00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:35.075
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> ‘I can follow her if you want.

00:00:35.779 --> 00:00:39.574
It will only cost you 7 dollars a day and expenses…’

00:00:40.048 --> 00:00:41.857
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘No, thank you,’

00:00:42.323 --> 00:00:43.561
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> interrupted Hartley.

00:00:44.058 --> 00:00:45.831
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘I only wanted the address.

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:47.835
How much is it?’

00:00:48.402 --> 00:00:49.610
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> ‘One day’s work,’

00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:50.979
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> said the detective.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.252
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> ‘Ten dollars.’

00:00:53.516 --> 00:00:54.942
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> Hartley paid the man.

00:00:55.447 --> 00:00:58.968
Then he left his office and took a tram to Broadway.

00:01:06.616 --> 00:01:12.078
After walking a short distance, he arrived at the building that he was looking for.

00:01:14.003 --> 00:01:20.567
He went up the stairs into her apartment and saw her standing by the window.

00:01:22.236 --> 00:01:24.740
Vivienne was about 21.

00:01:25.474 --> 00:01:29.362
Her hair was red gold, and her eyes were sea-blue.

00:01:30.614 --> 00:01:33.751
She was wearing a white top and a dark skirt.

00:01:34.556 --> 00:01:35.315
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘Vivienne,’

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.216
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> said Hartley angrily,

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.471
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘you didn’t answer my last letter.

00:01:40.326 --> 00:01:42.586
It took me a week to find your new address!

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.276
Why didn’t you answer me?

00:01:45.714 --> 00:01:48.627
You knew I was waiting to see you and hear from you.’